metacircular-univalent-unison-of-cubically-receptive-stateboxes-lines-8 = cons "## Unison: identity by content, many sounding as one" (cons "" (cons "The Unison language (Paul Chiusano, Rúnar Bjarnason and Arya Irani, Unison Computing) stores every definition by the hash of its syntax tree. A name is a label pointing at a hash; renaming rewrites nothing; dependencies refer to exactly the definitions they use. The paper's §10.8 cites it as the precedent for content-addressed definitions, and I have carried it for years as central to my thinking on interaction and languages." (cons "" nil)))
